# Apperture Core — Project rules

When working in this repository:

- **Agent instructions and non-negotiables:** Follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) at the repo root. Do not design around message handlers or a message bus; orchestration is workflow-centric. Single-tenant instance. Module/process isolation is a supported deployment option, not a current invariant (one Worker Host may host several modules today; do not assume a module is alone in its process and do not prevent running one per worker later). Portable workflow model: DTFx and Azure Durable Functions adapters are a design intent and are not implemented (today: SQL start-request queue with inline execution in the worker). **Never put epic/track/agent planning labels into operator-facing display names, seeds, notifications, settings help, or UI copy** (see AGENTS.md non-negotiable #6 and [.ai/playbooks/anti-patterns.md](.ai/playbooks/anti-patterns.md)).
- **Principles and anti-patterns:** See [.ai/playbooks/](.ai/playbooks/) for project map, principles, anti-patterns, module SDK, management service, and runtime portability.
- **Architecture:** Use [docs/01-architecture/](docs/01-architecture/) for control plane, instance plane, tenancy, workflows, and runtime backends.
- **Build, test and review procedure:** See [.ai/playbooks/dev-loop.md](.ai/playbooks/dev-loop.md). Focused local tests are for iteration; the required hosted CI always runs every test.
- **Repo layout:** `src/` by product area (Apperture.Cli, Apperture.ControlPlane, Apperture.ModuleSdk, Apperture.RuntimePlane, Apperture.RuntimeHost, Apperture.Shared). `tests/` contains unit, integration, arch, and e2e tests. `scripts/` holds dev and CI scripts. Add new code in the appropriate area; record decisions in `docs/02-decisions/` using the ADR template.
